Humana Coverage Policy: Imaging for Low Back Pain.
Lumbar MRI is covered when at least ONE red-flag indication is documented:
(a) Neurological deficit (motor weakness, dermatomal sensory loss, reflex changes, bowel/bladder dysfunction);
(b) History of malignancy with new back pain;
(c) Suspected infection (fever, IV drug use, immunocompromise);
(d) Suspected fracture (significant trauma, age >70, osteoporosis);
(e) Progressive neurological symptoms over weeks;
(f) Cauda equina symptoms.
Imaging requested for reassurance, return-to-sport clearance, or improving symptoms is not covered regardless of symptom duration or conservative therapy completion.

LCD L33611 — Oral Appliances for OSA: Replacement

Replacement of an existing oral appliance is covered when:
(a) The original device is documented as broken, lost, or no longer functional;
(b) Significant change in dental or skeletal anatomy (orthodontic treatment, extraction, restoration);
(c) Documented clinical re-evaluation showing the device is no longer effective at controlling AHI;
(d) Material wear documented by the fitting dentist.

Patient comfort or preference alone does NOT establish medical necessity for replacement. The original device must be functionally inadequate.

LCD L38394 — Pharmacogenomic Testing

Pharmacogenomic panel testing is covered when ALL of:
1. The patient has a current active medication management problem (treatment failure, intolerance, ADR, or planned initiation of a drug with known PGx-relevant interactions);
2. Specific genes tested are clinically actionable per CPIC or FDA guidance for the patient's medications;
3. Results will inform a documented treatment decision.

PROPHYLACTIC or screening pharmacogenomic testing without an active medication management problem is NOT covered. Testing 'in case' the patient ever needs PGx-relevant drugs is excluded regardless of panel sophistication or number of genes.
